  "title": "0: Sign in to Auth0",
  "nextTour": "1: Database Connections with Password Authentication",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "",
      "description": "## Authorize the Auth0 Labs Extension to access your default tenant\nBefore getting started, you’ll need to authorize the Auth0 Labs extension to access your default tenant.\n\n1. Select [this link](command:auth0.auth.signIn) to sign into your Auth0 account with the Auth0 extension.\n\n     A browser window will open requesting that you confirm that the code shown matches the one shown in the lower right hand side of your VSCode window.\n\n1.  Confirm that the values match, then select the **Confirm** button.\n\n     ![Confirm the values in VS Code](https://cdn.auth0.com/website/a0fun/v2/create-1.gif)   \n     ![Confirm the values in Auth0](https://cdn.auth0.com/website/a0fun/v2/create-0.gif)   \n     \n1.  The default tenant should already be selected (it starts with **dev-**) \n1.  Scroll down and select **Accept**. You should see a success message. You can close this browser tab now!\n\nNext, you’ll set up your tenant and local application configurations for this lab.",
      "line": 1
    }
  ]
}